{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Charts treats width and height differently:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"width is normally measured from the chart container's content box;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"height is a product decision supplied as pixels, an aspect ratio, or the\ncontainer's CSS content height;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scale factories infer domains while configured instances retain fixed domains;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Charts copies those scales and assigns responsive pixel ranges."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This keeps a definition stable while the same chart moves between a dashboard\ncard, a split pane, and a full-width report."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"container-responsive-width","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Container-responsive width"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mountChart"},{"type":"text","value":" or framework adapter options to follow the\ncontainer. The shared DOM host observes every container-owned content-box\ndimension and updates when its measured width or height changes. Padding and\nborders stay outside the chart scene."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const host = mountChart(element, {\n  definition,\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly downloads',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The container must have a resolvable content width. In grid and flex layouts,\nthe common requirement is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"min-width: 0"},{"type":"text","value":" on the grid or flex child:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".chart-card {\n  min-width: 0;\n}","lang":"css"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" only when an application deliberately owns fixed geometry, such\nas an export frame or a benchmark."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"height-and-aspect-ratio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Height and aspect ratio"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use one of these policies:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":": fixed product height in CSS pixels;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a positive, finite "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":": derive height from the measured content\nwidth;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"neither: follow a positive, finite CSS container content height, falling back\nto the host default of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"320"},{"type":"text","value":" until one is available."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not supply both as competing policies. A fixed height is usually more stable\nfor dashboards and scrolling pages. An aspect ratio is useful for editorial\nlayouts where the chart should scale as one visual block. Invalid ratios fall\nback to container height. A fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" does not disable height observation\nwhen CSS owns height."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Container-owned height must resolve independently of the chart surface, such\nas a fixed-height card, grid row, flex item, or remaining track. If the chart\nwould size a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height: auto"},{"type":"text","value":" container itself, supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":"\ninstead so the surface is not also its own resize input."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"automatic-guide-space","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic guide space"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"margin"},{"type":"text","value":" for normal charts. The scene solver reserves the minimum space\nrequired by:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"formatted tick labels;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rotated tick bounds;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"first and last tick overhang;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"axis titles;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"legends;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"inherited font metrics in a DOM host."}]}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"responsive-long-labels-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"responsive-long-labels","data-collapsed-indexes":"[1]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/chart.ts\",\"environment\":\"charts\",\"files\":{\"/src/chart.ts\":\"import { barX, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\\nimport { rows } from './data'\\n\\nexport default defineChart({\\n  marks: [\\n    barX(rows, {\\n      x: 'weeklyRequests',\\n      y: 'feature',\\n      fill: '#7c3aed',\\n      inset: 1,\\n    }),\\n  ],\\n  scales: {\\n    x: {\\n      scale: scaleLinear,\\n      nice: true,\\n      grid: true,\\n      axis: { ticks: { count: 5 }, label: 'Weekly requests' },\\n    },\\n    y: {\\n      scale: () => scaleBand<string>().padding(0.1),\\n    },\\n  },\\n})\",\"/src/data.ts\":\"export const rows = [\\n  { feature: 'Self-service account recovery', weeklyRequests: 128 },\\n  { feature: 'Saved searches and alerting', weeklyRequests: 95 },\\n  { feature: 'Audit log export', weeklyRequests: 72 },\\n  { feature: 'Custom retention policies', weeklyRequests: 44 },\\n  { feature: 'Role-based access controls', weeklyRequests: 31 },\\n]\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { barX, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barX(rows, {\n      x: 'weeklyRequests',\n      y: 'feature',\n      fill: '#7c3aed',\n      inset: 1,\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: { ticks: { count: 5 }, label: 'Weekly requests' },\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand<string>().padding(0.1),\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"group=responsive-long-labels env=charts file=/src/chart.ts entry","title":"/src/chart.ts","file":"/src/chart.ts"},{"type":"code","value":"export const rows = [\n  { feature: 'Self-service account recovery', weeklyRequests: 128 },\n  { feature: 'Saved searches and alerting', weeklyRequests: 95 },\n  { feature: 'Audit log export', weeklyRequests: 72 },\n  { feature: 'Custom retention policies', weeklyRequests: 44 },\n  { feature: 'Role-based access controls', weeklyRequests: 31 },\n]","lang":"ts","meta":"group=responsive-long-labels file=/src/data.ts collapsed","title":"/src/data.ts","file":"/src/data.ts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An explicit side locks only that side:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"margin: {\n  left: 96\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"margin: 0"},{"type":"text","value":" locks every side and is appropriate for guide-free sparklines.\nAxis labels thin automatically after candidate generation and optional\nrotation. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis.ticks.spacing"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"axis.tickLabels.rotate"},{"type":"text","value":", hard-kept labels,\nor a different representation when labels compete for the same axis space."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/bar-horizontal-ranking/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open the full horizontal-ranking catalog case"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-measurement","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text measurement"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static scenes use deterministic text estimates. DOM and framework SVG hosts\nmeasure painted text with the inherited container font and relayout after web\nfonts finish loading."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureText"},{"type":"text","value":" only when another renderer or layout system owns text\nmeasurement. It runs synchronously during scene compilation and receives the\ntext plus the resolved font family, style, stretch, size, weight, letter\nspacing, direction, locale, font scale, anchor, and baseline. It returns the\npainted box relative to the requested origin. A host that loads fonts or\nmeasures them asynchronously owns that readiness lifecycle and renders the\nscene again when its synchronous metrics change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The resolved geometry is available after every render:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const scene = host.getScene()\n\nscene.margin\nscene.chart\nscene.scales","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scene.chart"},{"type":"text","value":" to align application-owned overlays. Do not calculate a\nparallel plot rectangle from guessed margins."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"deterministic-server-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deterministic server output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A server cannot measure a future browser container. Supply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" when\nthe initial SVG must have deterministic geometry:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  initialWidth={640}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads\"\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client adopts the real container width after hydration. Use the same\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" for all requests that render the same layout; do not derive it\nfrom browser-only APIs on the server."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./ssr-and-hydration.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR and Hydration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the complete lifecycle."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"responsive-construction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive construction"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most data transforms should depend only on application data. The responsive\nbuilder receives the full scene width and height, so it can choose breakpoints,\ntick counts, or a surface-relative representation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Those values are not the final inner plot bounds. Automatic guides and legends\nresolve "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scene.chart"},{"type":"text","value":" after the builder returns. Exact plot-space collision,\nbinning, or label placement belongs in a custom mark's render phase, which\nreceives the final chart bounds and resolved scales, or in an application\noverlay driven by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRender"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"function summarizeRows(rows: Input['rows']) {\n  return summarize(rows)\n}\n\nfunction createDefinition(rows: Input['rows']) {\n  const summary = summarizeRows(rows)\n\n  return defineChart(({ width }) =>\n    buildResponsiveSpec(summary, {\n      compact: width < 480,\n    }),\n  )\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a deliberately guide-free "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"margin: 0"},{"type":"text","value":" scene, the full surface and inner\nplot can coincide. Do not assume that equivalence for ordinary automatic\nlayout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive relayout commits immediately even when animation is enabled for\ndata updates. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation: { resize: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" only when size interpolation is\nintentional."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"./dynamic-data-and-animation.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Data and Animation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide explains\nthe two phases. The "},{"type":"link","href":"../concepts/scales-and-d3.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"D3 integration contract"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nexplains why application code should not set positional pixel ranges."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"responsive-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The container can shrink because its grid or flex child uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"min-width: 0"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Width is omitted unless fixed geometry is intentional."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Height or aspect ratio is an explicit product choice."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scale domains remain semantic and independent from pixels."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic margins are enabled unless the chart is deliberately guide-free."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Long labels are tested at the smallest supported width."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overlays use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scene.chart"},{"type":"text","value":", not duplicated margin math."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR uses a deterministic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Final plot-space work reads custom-mark render bounds or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scene.chart"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"container-responsive-width","text":"Container-responsive width","level":2},{"id":"height-and-aspect-ratio","text":"Height and aspect ratio","level":2},{"id":"automatic-guide-space","text":"Automatic guide space","level":2},{"id":"text-measurement","text":"Text measurement","level":2},{"id":"deterministic-server-output","text":"Deterministic server output","level":2},{"id":"responsive-construction","text":"Responsive construction","level":2},{"id":"responsive-checklist","text":"Responsive checklist","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Charts treats width and height differently:\n\n- width is normally measured from the chart container's content box;\n- height is a product decision supplied as pixels, an aspect ratio, or the\n  container's CSS content height;\n- scale factories infer domains while configured instances retain fixed domains;\n- TanStack Charts copies those scales and assigns responsive pixel ranges.\n\nThis keeps a definition stable while the same chart moves between a dashboard\ncard, a split pane, and a full-width report.\n\n## Container-responsive width\n\nOmit `width` from `mountChart` or framework adapter options to follow the\ncontainer. The shared DOM host observes every container-owned content-box\ndimension and updates when its measured width or height changes. Padding and\nborders stay outside the chart scene.\n\n```ts\nconst host = mountChart(element, {\n  definition,\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly downloads',\n})\n```\n\nThe container must have a resolvable content width. In grid and flex layouts,\nthe common requirement is `min-width: 0` on the grid or flex child:\n\n```css\n.chart-card {\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n```\n\nSupply `width` only when an application deliberately owns fixed geometry, such\nas an export frame or a benchmark.\n\n## Height and aspect ratio\n\nUse one of these policies:\n\n- `height`: fixed product height in CSS pixels;\n- a positive, finite `aspectRatio`: derive height from the measured content\n  width;\n- neither: follow a positive, finite CSS container content height, falling back\n  to the host default of `320` until one is available.\n\nDo not supply both as competing policies. A fixed height is usually more stable\nfor dashboards and scrolling pages. An aspect ratio is useful for editorial\nlayouts where the chart should scale as one visual block. Invalid ratios fall\nback to container height. A fixed `width` does not disable height observation\nwhen CSS owns height.\n\nContainer-owned height must resolve independently of the chart surface, such\nas a fixed-height card, grid row, flex item, or remaining track. If the chart\nwould size a `height: auto` container itself, supply `height` or `aspectRatio`\ninstead so the surface is not also its own resize input.\n\n## Automatic guide space\n\nOmit `margin` for normal charts. The scene solver reserves the minimum space\nrequired by:\n\n- formatted tick labels;\n- rotated tick bounds;\n- first and last tick overhang;\n- axis titles;\n- legends;\n- inherited font metrics in a DOM host.\n\n```ts group=responsive-long-labels env=charts file=/src/chart.ts entry\nimport { barX, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barX(rows, {\n      x: 'weeklyRequests',\n      y: 'feature',\n      fill: '#7c3aed',\n      inset: 1,\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: { ticks: { count: 5 }, label: 'Weekly requests' },\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand<string>().padding(0.1),\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```ts group=responsive-long-labels file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport const rows = [\n  { feature: 'Self-service account recovery', weeklyRequests: 128 },\n  { feature: 'Saved searches and alerting', weeklyRequests: 95 },\n  { feature: 'Audit log export', weeklyRequests: 72 },\n  { feature: 'Custom retention policies', weeklyRequests: 44 },\n  { feature: 'Role-based access controls', weeklyRequests: 31 },\n]\n```\n\nAn explicit side locks only that side:\n\n```ts\nmargin: {\n  left: 96\n}\n```\n\n`margin: 0` locks every side and is appropriate for guide-free sparklines.\nAxis labels thin automatically after candidate generation and optional\nrotation. Use `axis.ticks.spacing`, `axis.tickLabels.rotate`, hard-kept labels,\nor a different representation when labels compete for the same axis space.\n\n[Open the full horizontal-ranking catalog case](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/bar-horizontal-ranking/).\n\n## Text measurement\n\nStatic scenes use deterministic text estimates. DOM and framework SVG hosts\nmeasure painted text with the inherited container font and relayout after web\nfonts finish loading.\n\nUse `measureText` only when another renderer or layout system owns text\nmeasurement. It runs synchronously during scene compilation and receives the\ntext plus the resolved font family, style, stretch, size, weight, letter\nspacing, direction, locale, font scale, anchor, and baseline. It returns the\npainted box relative to the requested origin. A host that loads fonts or\nmeasures them asynchronously owns that readiness lifecycle and renders the\nscene again when its synchronous metrics change.\n\nThe resolved geometry is available after every render:\n\n```ts\nconst scene = host.getScene()\n\nscene.margin\nscene.chart\nscene.scales\n```\n\nUse `scene.chart` to align application-owned overlays. Do not calculate a\nparallel plot rectangle from guessed margins.\n\n## Deterministic server output\n\nA server cannot measure a future browser container. Supply `initialWidth` when\nthe initial SVG must have deterministic geometry:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  initialWidth={640}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe client adopts the real container width after hydration. Use the same\n`initialWidth` for all requests that render the same layout; do not derive it\nfrom browser-only APIs on the server.\n\nSee [SSR and Hydration](./ssr-and-hydration.md) for the complete lifecycle.\n\n## Responsive construction\n\nMost data transforms should depend only on application data. The responsive\nbuilder receives the full scene width and height, so it can choose breakpoints,\ntick counts, or a surface-relative representation.\n\nThose values are not the final inner plot bounds. Automatic guides and legends\nresolve `scene.chart` after the builder returns. Exact plot-space collision,\nbinning, or label placement belongs in a custom mark's render phase, which\nreceives the final chart bounds and resolved scales, or in an application\noverlay driven by `onRender`.\n\n```ts\nfunction summarizeRows(rows: Input['rows']) {\n  return summarize(rows)\n}\n\nfunction createDefinition(rows: Input['rows']) {\n  const summary = summarizeRows(rows)\n\n  return defineChart(({ width }) =>\n    buildResponsiveSpec(summary, {\n      compact: width < 480,\n    }),\n  )\n}\n```\n\nFor a deliberately guide-free `margin: 0` scene, the full surface and inner\nplot can coincide. Do not assume that equivalence for ordinary automatic\nlayout.\n\nResponsive relayout commits immediately even when animation is enabled for\ndata updates. Set `svgAnimation: { resize: true }` only when size interpolation is\nintentional.\n\nThe [Dynamic Data and Animation](./dynamic-data-and-animation.md) guide explains\nthe two phases. The [D3 integration contract](../concepts/scales-and-d3.md)\nexplains why application code should not set positional pixel ranges.\n\n## Responsive checklist\n\n- The container can shrink because its grid or flex child uses `min-width: 0`.\n- Width is omitted unless fixed geometry is intentional.\n- Height or aspect ratio is an explicit product choice.\n- Scale domains remain semantic and independent from pixels.\n- Automatic margins are enabled unless the chart is deliberately guide-free.\n- Long labels are tested at the smallest supported width.\n- Overlays use `scene.chart`, not duplicated margin math.\n- SSR uses a deterministic `initialWidth`.\n- Final plot-space work reads custom-mark render bounds or `scene.chart`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Responsive Charts\ndescription: Size charts from their containers while preserving readable guides, deterministic SSR, and application-controlled height.\n---\n\nTanStack Charts treats width and height differently:\n\n- width is normally measured from the chart container's content box;\n- height is a product decision supplied as pixels, an aspect ratio, or the\n  container's CSS content height;\n- scale factories infer domains while configured instances retain fixed domains;\n- TanStack Charts copies those scales and assigns responsive pixel ranges.\n\nThis keeps a definition stable while the same chart moves between a dashboard\ncard, a split pane, and a full-width report.\n\n## Container-responsive width\n\nOmit `width` from `mountChart` or framework adapter options to follow the\ncontainer. The shared DOM host observes every container-owned content-box\ndimension and updates when its measured width or height changes. Padding and\nborders stay outside the chart scene.\n\n```ts\nconst host = mountChart(element, {\n  definition,\n  height: 320,\n  ariaLabel: 'Weekly downloads',\n})\n```\n\nThe container must have a resolvable content width. In grid and flex layouts,\nthe common requirement is `min-width: 0` on the grid or flex child:\n\n```css\n.chart-card {\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n```\n\nSupply `width` only when an application deliberately owns fixed geometry, such\nas an export frame or a benchmark.\n\n## Height and aspect ratio\n\nUse one of these policies:\n\n- `height`: fixed product height in CSS pixels;\n- a positive, finite `aspectRatio`: derive height from the measured content\n  width;\n- neither: follow a positive, finite CSS container content height, falling back\n  to the host default of `320` until one is available.\n\nDo not supply both as competing policies. A fixed height is usually more stable\nfor dashboards and scrolling pages. An aspect ratio is useful for editorial\nlayouts where the chart should scale as one visual block. Invalid ratios fall\nback to container height. A fixed `width` does not disable height observation\nwhen CSS owns height.\n\nContainer-owned height must resolve independently of the chart surface, such\nas a fixed-height card, grid row, flex item, or remaining track. If the chart\nwould size a `height: auto` container itself, supply `height` or `aspectRatio`\ninstead so the surface is not also its own resize input.\n\n## Automatic guide space\n\nOmit `margin` for normal charts. The scene solver reserves the minimum space\nrequired by:\n\n- formatted tick labels;\n- rotated tick bounds;\n- first and last tick overhang;\n- axis titles;\n- legends;\n- inherited font metrics in a DOM host.\n\n```ts group=responsive-long-labels env=charts file=/src/chart.ts entry\nimport { barX, defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { rows } from './data'\n\nexport default defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    barX(rows, {\n      x: 'weeklyRequests',\n      y: 'feature',\n      fill: '#7c3aed',\n      inset: 1,\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: { ticks: { count: 5 }, label: 'Weekly requests' },\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: () => scaleBand<string>().padding(0.1),\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```ts group=responsive-long-labels file=/src/data.ts collapsed\nexport const rows = [\n  { feature: 'Self-service account recovery', weeklyRequests: 128 },\n  { feature: 'Saved searches and alerting', weeklyRequests: 95 },\n  { feature: 'Audit log export', weeklyRequests: 72 },\n  { feature: 'Custom retention policies', weeklyRequests: 44 },\n  { feature: 'Role-based access controls', weeklyRequests: 31 },\n]\n```\n\nAn explicit side locks only that side:\n\n```ts\nmargin: {\n  left: 96\n}\n```\n\n`margin: 0` locks every side and is appropriate for guide-free sparklines.\nAxis labels thin automatically after candidate generation and optional\nrotation. Use `axis.ticks.spacing`, `axis.tickLabels.rotate`, hard-kept labels,\nor a different representation when labels compete for the same axis space.\n\n[Open the full horizontal-ranking catalog case](https://tanstack.com/charts/catalog/bar-horizontal-ranking/).\n\n## Text measurement\n\nStatic scenes use deterministic text estimates. DOM and framework SVG hosts\nmeasure painted text with the inherited container font and relayout after web\nfonts finish loading.\n\nUse `measureText` only when another renderer or layout system owns text\nmeasurement. It runs synchronously during scene compilation and receives the\ntext plus the resolved font family, style, stretch, size, weight, letter\nspacing, direction, locale, font scale, anchor, and baseline. It returns the\npainted box relative to the requested origin. A host that loads fonts or\nmeasures them asynchronously owns that readiness lifecycle and renders the\nscene again when its synchronous metrics change.\n\nThe resolved geometry is available after every render:\n\n```ts\nconst scene = host.getScene()\n\nscene.margin\nscene.chart\nscene.scales\n```\n\nUse `scene.chart` to align application-owned overlays. Do not calculate a\nparallel plot rectangle from guessed margins.\n\n## Deterministic server output\n\nA server cannot measure a future browser container. Supply `initialWidth` when\nthe initial SVG must have deterministic geometry:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  initialWidth={640}\n  height={320}\n  ariaLabel=\"Weekly downloads\"\n/>\n```\n\nThe client adopts the real container width after hydration. Use the same\n`initialWidth` for all requests that render the same layout; do not derive it\nfrom browser-only APIs on the server.\n\nSee [SSR and Hydration](./ssr-and-hydration.md) for the complete lifecycle.\n\n## Responsive construction\n\nMost data transforms should depend only on application data. The responsive\nbuilder receives the full scene width and height, so it can choose breakpoints,\ntick counts, or a surface-relative representation.\n\nThose values are not the final inner plot bounds. Automatic guides and legends\nresolve `scene.chart` after the builder returns. Exact plot-space collision,\nbinning, or label placement belongs in a custom mark's render phase, which\nreceives the final chart bounds and resolved scales, or in an application\noverlay driven by `onRender`.\n\n```ts\nfunction summarizeRows(rows: Input['rows']) {\n  return summarize(rows)\n}\n\nfunction createDefinition(rows: Input['rows']) {\n  const summary = summarizeRows(rows)\n\n  return defineChart(({ width }) =>\n    buildResponsiveSpec(summary, {\n      compact: width < 480,\n    }),\n  )\n}\n```\n\nFor a deliberately guide-free `margin: 0` scene, the full surface and inner\nplot can coincide. Do not assume that equivalence for ordinary automatic\nlayout.\n\nResponsive relayout commits immediately even when animation is enabled for\ndata updates. Set `svgAnimation: { resize: true }` only when size interpolation is\nintentional.\n\nThe [Dynamic Data and Animation](./dynamic-data-and-animation.md) guide explains\nthe two phases. The [D3 integration contract](../concepts/scales-and-d3.md)\nexplains why application code should not set positional pixel ranges.\n\n## Responsive checklist\n\n- The container can shrink because its grid or flex child uses `min-width: 0`.\n- Width is omitted unless fixed geometry is intentional.\n- Height or aspect ratio is an explicit product choice.\n- Scale domains remain semantic and independent from pixels.\n- Automatic margins are enabled unless the chart is deliberately guide-free.\n- Long labels are tested at the smallest supported width.\n- Overlays use `scene.chart`, not duplicated margin math.\n- SSR uses a deterministic `initialWidth`.\n- Final plot-space work reads custom-mark render bounds or `scene.chart`.\n"}
